                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/294: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-26T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26, 1922—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 26—12:05
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>102. Department’s telegram number 80, June 3, 1 p.m. Foreign Office states
                    Italian Government has no objection to Government of the United States
                    circularizing the powers as proposed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
